2:T728,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to have a kitchen installed near me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough typical UK guide, installation-only labour may be around £2,000 to £5,000, while a complete kitchen project may be around £8,000 to £20,000 or more. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does kitchen installation include plumbing and electrics?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sometimes, but not always. Some fitters include basic connections while others charge separately or arrange for other trades. Check the quote for plumbing, electrical alterations, lighting and appliance connections."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to buy a kitchen separately and pay a fitter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be, but the overall cost and result depend on delivery, measurements, missing parts and the installation scope. A supply-and-fit quote may be easier to compare, while separate supply gives you more control over product choices."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a kitchen installation take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A straightforward replacement may take around one to two weeks, but this is only a rough guide. Structural changes, re-plumbing, rewiring, bespoke worktops, delayed deliveries and remedial work can extend the programme."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I check in a kitchen fitting quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Check the total price, VAT, payment stages, timescale, waste removal, preparation, worktops, appliances, plumbing, electrics, tiling, flooring, decorating, exclusions and the process for agreeing variations."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-installation-near-me-cost","d"]
